      "functional_impact_measured": "PMC10016038: SNAP-GIPR in INS-1 832/3 beta cells \u2014 receptor trafficking and internalization measured following GIP(1-42) stimulation; surface display confirmed; receptor function (agonist-driven internalization) preserved. PMC3296735: surface blot confirmed surface expression of HA-tagged GIPR. PMC13544220: cell-impermeant SNAP probe confirmed plasma membrane localization.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "The signal peptide spans residues 1-21 (authoritative topology); the mature N-terminus begins at residue 22 (R). An N-terminal tag inserted 'directly downstream of the signal peptide' therefore sits at insert_after_residue=21, placing the tag between Q21 and R22. This is confirmed by Python: res(21)='Q', res(22)='R'. Seven independent publications using at least five distinct tag types (HA, myc, SNAP, SNAP-f, FLAG+mNG, 3xHA, HiBiT) all report N-terminal extracellular tagging of full-length membrane-anchored GIPR at this junction. The site is extracellular (residue 22 begins the 22-136 extracellular domain), well clear of TM1 (starts at 137, >115 residues away), and the tag is on the extracellular face. Surface expression and agonist-driven receptor trafficking were confirmed in multiple cell systems. The best-validated construct (SNAP-GIPR, PMC10016038) demonstrated both surface display and functional internalization in response to GIP(1-42) in pancreatic beta cells. Multiple independent studies inserted epitope or self-labeling tags immediately downstream of the GIPR signal peptide (residues 1-21), placing the tag at the extracellular N-terminus of the mature receptor. PMC3296735: HA (YPYDVPDYA) inserted directly downstream of the signal peptide; surface expression confirmed by surface blot. PMC4156404: myc-tag introduced immediately downstream of the predicted signal peptide; surface detection confirmed. PMC7526454: N-terminal 3X-HA and N-terminal SNAP-tag constructs used for internalization assays. PMC7317972: SNAP-GIPR (Cisbio) used for functional and binding studies. PMC10016038: SNAP-GIPR stably expressed in INS-1 832/3 beta cells; receptor trafficking and agonist-stimulated internalization measured, confirming surface display and functional response. PMC13485621: FLAG+mNeonGreen at N-terminus for expression and trafficking studies. PMC13544220: SNAP-f tag replacing endogenous signal peptide; surface expression confirmed by cell-impermeant SNAP probe in AD293 cells. [validation: surface_and_function; position: inferred; source: paper; cited_tag_residue: 21; entailment_verified: True]",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 22412906,
          "citation": "PMID 22412906",
          "claim": "For N-terminally HA-tagged constructs, overlapping PCR mutagenesis was used to insert the HA epitope (YPYDVPDYA) directly downstream of the GIPR and GLP1R putative signal peptide sequences on their N-termini."
        }
      ],
